From: Vihan Aggarwal <mooimacow1234567@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:23:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Data loader: read the first shard's partial-index span
 before the first batch, the rest after

The timed run's first fetch read the whole 200 MB first shard before batch 0 (with all 8 ranks
reading the same file at once), although the first ~45 batches only use tokens below the
partial index's 6M. That span (12 MB) is now read first; the index thread reads the remaining
188 MB, still on the clock, before its full scan. First batch on CPU, with pre-faulted buffers
standing in for the cached pinned blocks: 34-50 ms -> 12.5-12.8 ms.

While on the partial index, a document must end at a BOS the index holds, so no token past it is
read before it is loaded. A batch that would need more raises PartialIndexExhausted, and
next_batch waits for the full index and builds it again. The record's loader instead read the
end of the partial index as the end of the shard: a wrong document end, then a StopIteration
that skipped the rest of the shard. Runs never get there (the host stays a few steps ahead of
the GPU), but the stream is now the intended one even when batches outrun the scan.

tools/tests/test_token_stream_identical.py runs this loader without help against the record's
loader held to its intended stream: the whole 1194-step schedule and the validation identical,
with the wait taken during the test.

